{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461850-vampire-the-masquerade-v5-the-kiasyd","id":1461850,"title":"Vampire The Masquerade [V5] The Kiasyd","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-28T12:10:52-07:00","id":1461850,"title":"Vampire The Masquerade [V5] The Kiasyd","content":"No mention of the &quot;Kiasyd&quot; bloodline in V5. They are my favorite bloodline and I believe they are also the preferred bloodline of many people. I wonder if anyone has any news if they will come out in any future books. Or if there is any way to send this type of question to the creators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T12:38:52-07:00","id":1461852,"title":"","content":"Probably not, and I like 'em too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T13:27:07-07:00","id":1461857,"title":"","content":"I like everything about them but the Discipline. I don't think it was that thought out. I understand the instinct to give each new clan/bloodline it's own discipline, and a set three disciplines in general. For Kiasyd I think it would be better to give them a cross between protean and Vicissitude with an emphasis on shape changeling. Mytherceria never really did it for me. Changing their own appearance, turning into animals, it feels more Fae. Fae Sight to see other changelings for level one, the Vicissitude level two self only no roll, turn into a tree that can sleep through he day for level three, protean level 4 (maybe a falcon instead of a bat), absorb memories for level 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 09-28-2021, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T13:50:53-07:00","id":1461859,"title":"","content":"I disagree with the idea of making it a shapechanging discipline, but pretty much agree that Mytherceria is a lacking discipline.<br /> <br /> Fae aren't shapechangers with that frequency and especially not in the WoD, and it would inevitably need hints to CtD even if not outright embracing crossover. It should deal with dreams, pacts, enhancing and scrambling perceptions. I particularly like the idea behind the Chanjeling Ward, but not the execution. And the Riddle Fantastique is lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T14:02:41-07:00","id":1461861,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the Changeling Ward the least, but I don't see them changing to my way either. Took a few editing passes but I think I'll write mine down for my own games. I think the tortured nature, the flaws of Iron and self loathing plus the weird looks are all good. What were the other two Disciplines they have? was it Obtenebration and ??<br /> <br /> I like Dominate, but feel they should have a physical Discipline, maybe Celerity? drop the Obtenebration...lol I'm sure lots of fans will hate my version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 09-28-2021, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T14:37:03-07:00","id":1461869,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Obtenebration is there just to remind you they're a Lasombra bloodline. As much as I like the Discipline, I agree with you, it doesn't belong in the Kyasid and Celerity would fit them better. I'd like to see your take on Mytherceria, maybe I'll do mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T14:39:03-07:00","id":1461870,"title":"","content":"I like the Kiasyd because in Scottish mythology vampires are considered part of the fae folk and I love the idea of there being a bunch of Kiasyd dotted around Scotland and that gave rise to those myths.There is already a bunch of influence from Eastern European vampires and Western European revenants folklore in the different clans and bloodlines so why not do the same for celtic as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T14:40:11-07:00","id":1461871,"title":"","content":"I believe Mytherceria can be made as amalgam powers. The ward and the riddle are powers that for me are the Kiasyd's signature. As well as the power of fairy vision.<br /> This could be accompanied by &quot;Loresheets&quot; such as &quot;Fairy Blood&quot; or &quot;Marconius Bloodline&quot;.<br /> I think the authors could talk about the bloodline, even a little, so we can know if they will exist or not.. The lack of information about the bloodline is something that saddens me a lot. They really are my favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","user":"YueSidhe","date":". 09-28-2021, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T15:22:43-07:00","id":1461879,"title":"","content":"They exist, they're not writing off material in that way yet. Sine the Sabbat is in its current state, the surviving Kyasid are probably Anarchs or Autarkis.<br /> <br /> The only thing really in our way is making their Bane and Compulsion in mechanical terms and the discipline. Since Mytherceria would be an Amalgam (I was thinking in V20 terms before, that's what I play), Their spread should probably be Celerity, Dominate and Oblivion if you want something fitting, or Dominate, Oblivion and Potence if you want to keep the emphasis on being a Lasombra bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T19:14:44-07:00","id":1461901,"title":"","content":"Oblivion fits Kiasyd wonderfully if the &quot;fae&quot; to which they're akin are some sort of eldritch, underground people, hence they'd also make a marvellous VtR Nosferatu bloodline. Mytherceria features several sensory abilities, so Auspex could be a suitable replacement and it could feature in amalgams for resonance removal and knowledge theft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T19:21:59-07:00","id":1461903,"title":"","content":"I think most of the sensory powers of Mytherceria could just be fae-flavored interpretations of existing Auspex powers. Aura Absorption and Chanjelin Ward would work as Oblivion ceremonies, and Riddle Phantastique could just be a new Dominate power, or a Dominate/Obfuscate amalgam like Dementation is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T20:21:15-07:00","id":1461907,"title":"","content":"Lore-wise the fae related to the Kyasid is already established as the Changeling from CtD, so I don't think that Oblivion fits in this sense as an &quot;official-like&quot; option. I do agree that it works very well as a combination of Auspex and Dominate powers/amalgams. But then the lack of Auspex would hurt them, and I see some options for a Discipline spread:<br /> <br /> Traditional Spread: Auspex, Dominate and Oblivion. It keeps the original spread with all its pros and cons.<br /> Optional Spread: Auspex, Celerity and Dominate. It gives them a physical Discipline and I still find Oblivion not that fitting for them except for screaming Lasombra.<br /> Middle Ground: Auspex, Dominate, Potence. It isn't as fitting as Celerity, but is the Physical of their parent clan.<br /> <br /> Personally I would change the powers instead of just adapting them, but I think this also goes against creating an &quot;official-like&quot; option. Folderol and Fae Sight are ok powers, more circumstantial but empowered by the lack of rolls, but Aura Absorption is kind of lame. Chanjeling Ward and The Riddle Fantastique are better on concept than the actual effects they got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T21:56:27-07:00","id":1461914,"title":"","content":"For other options have a look at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/262488/Clanbook-Kiasyd\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...lanbook-Kiasyd</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T06:12:05-07:00","id":1461948,"title":"","content":"I remember someone wrote up a Kyasid that was a type of Duskborn that really focused on the alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T09:36:44-07:00","id":1461971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461850-vampire-the-masquerade-v5-the-kiasyd?p=1461907#post1461907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore-wise the fae related to the Kyasid is already established as the Changeling from CtD, so I don't think that Oblivion fits in this sense as an &amp;quot;official-like&amp;quot; option. I do agree that it works very well as a combination of Auspex and Dominate powers/amalgams. But then the lack of Auspex would hurt them, and I see some options for a Discipline spread:<br /> <br /> Traditional Spread: Auspex, Dominate and Oblivion. It keeps the original spread with all its pros and cons.<br /> Optional Spread: Auspex, Celerity and Dominate. It gives them a physical Discipline and I still find Oblivion not that fitting for them except for screaming Lasombra.<br /> Middle Ground: Auspex, Dominate, Potence. It isn't as fitting as Celerity, but is the Physical of their parent clan.<br /> <br /> Personally I would change the powers instead of just adapting them, but I think this also goes against creating an &amp;quot;official-like&amp;quot; option. Folderol and Fae Sight are ok powers, more circumstantial but empowered by the lack of rolls, but Aura Absorption is kind of lame. Chanjeling Ward and The Riddle Fantastique are better on concept than the actual effects they got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore wise, the kyasid are linked especially to the sluaghs, which are underground, shadow beings. So obtenebration matches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T11:39:48-07:00","id":1461987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461850-vampire-the-masquerade-v5-the-kiasyd?p=1461971#post1461971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore wise, the kyasid are linked especially to the sluaghs, which are underground, shadow beings. So obtenebration matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Sluagh are more linked to Animalism and Obfuscate than Obtenebration, even Viscissitude or Protean due to their bodies. But I'd still say that they should get general fae links before getting specific Sluagh links.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was talking about fitting for Mytherceria powers, not for the clan spread. For the clan spread the official answer is Obtenebration/Oblivion anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:34:12-07:00","id":1462064,"title":"","content":"Always thought it strange that the Kiasyd aren't the ones who had Chimestry because the idea of chimerical creations is such a part of Changeling. Now granted when both the Ravnos and Kiasyd came out in Vampire, Changeling was several years away so they didn't really have a way to coherently tie them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}